\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{8\\pi}{5}\\right)}$","choice2":"$\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)}$","choice3":"$\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}\\right)}$","choice4":"$\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}{5}\\right)}$","choice5":"$\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{4}\\right)}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s recall the double-angle formula for cosine:</p>\n<p>\\[\n2 \\cos^2 x - 1 = \\cos 2x\n\\]</p>\n<p>Substituting $x={\\dfrac{4\\pi}{5}}$ into the above, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n2\\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}{5}\\right)} -1 \t&=\\cos{\\left(2 \\cdot \\dfrac{4\\pi}{5}\\right)} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{8\\pi}{5}\\right)}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":831,"name":"The Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"},"example":{"id":3667,"title":"Using Alternative Forms of Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions "},"group":{"id":55310,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14275038,"answer":{"id":62413463,"cread":"2026-10-17T00:49:11.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12037},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62413472,"created":"2026-10-17T00:49:28.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12878,"number":4,"createdStr":"Sat, Oct 17th @ 12:49 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":24341,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3667,"text":"<p>Express $1 - 2\\sin^2 \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}\\right) $ as a single trigonometric ratio.</p>\n","choice1":"$\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi} 5\\right)}$","choice2":"$\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi} 5\\right)}$","choice3":"$-\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi} 5\\right)}$","choice4":"$\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi} {10}\\right)}$","choice5":"$-\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi} {10}\\right)}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s recall the double-angle formula for cosine:</p>\n<p>\\[\n1 - 2\\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n\\]</p>\n<p>Substituting $x={\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}}$ into the above, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n1 - 2\\sin^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}\\right)} \t&=\\cos{\\left(2 \\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{5}\\right)} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":831,"name":"The Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"},"example":{"id":3667,"title":"Using Alternative Forms of Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions "},"group":{"id":44218,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14275038,"answer":{"id":62413472,"cread":"2026-10-17T00:49:28.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12878},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":3668,"number":3,"title":"Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula","answers":[{"id":62413481,"created":"2026-10-17T00:49:48.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"\\\\frac{3}{4}\"]","timeElapsed":12986,"number":5,"createdStr":"Sat, Oct 17th @ 12:49 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":275706,"format":"FR","difficulty":3,"exampleId":3668,"text":"Find the <strong>exact</strong> value of the expression below.","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":"\\newline\n\n$\\cos^4({15^{\\circ}}) - 2\\cos^2({15^{\\circ}}) \\sin^2({15^{\\circ}}) + \\sin^4({15^{\\circ}})=$\n[\n    answer: \\dfrac{3}{4};\n    type: number;\n    width: 40;\n    margin-left: 4;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: frac, exp, sqrt;\n]\n","explanation":"<p>First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\cos^4({15^{\\circ}}) - 2\\cos^2({15^{\\circ}}) \\sin^2({15^{\\circ}}) + \\sin^4({15^{\\circ}})\n&= \\left(\\cos^2({15^{\\circ}}) - \\sin^2({15^{\\circ}})\\right)^2\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Now, let&#39;s recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\\[\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n\\]</p>\n<p>Substituting $x={15^{\\circ}}$ into the above, we get\n\\begin{align}\n\\cos^2({15^{\\circ}}) - \\sin^2({15^{\\circ}})\n&= \\cos{\\left(2 \\cdot 15^{\\circ}\\right)} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\cos({30^{\\circ}}) \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Finally, we obtain \n\\begin{align*}\n\\left(\\cos^2({15^{\\circ}}) - \\sin^2({15^{\\circ}})\\right)^2 &= \\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2\n= \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{\\dfrac{3}{4}}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":831,"name":"The Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"},"example":{"id":3668,"title":"Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula"},"group":{"id":89973,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14275038,"answer":{"id":62413481,"cread":"2026-10-17T00:49:48.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["\\frac{3}{4}"],"timeElapsed":12986},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"newline":true},{"text":"$\\cos^4({15^{\\circ}}) - 2\\cos^2({15^{\\circ}}) \\sin^2({15^{\\circ}}) + \\sin^4({15^{\\circ}})=$\n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"\\dfrac{3}{4}","type":"number","width":40,"margin":{"left":4,"right":1},"buttons":["frac","exp","sqrt"]}}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62413489,"created":"2026-10-17T00:50:09.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15467,"number":6,"createdStr":"Sat, Oct 17th @ 12:50 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":7470,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3668,"text":"<p>Find the exact value of $\\cos^2{(75^{\\circ})} - \\sin^2{(75^{\\circ})}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\n","choice2":"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\n","choice3":"$\\dfrac{1}{2}$\n","choice4":"$-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$","choice5":"$-\\dfrac{1}{2}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s recall the double-angle formula for cosine:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\cos^2{x} - \\sin^2{x} = \\cos 2x\n\\]</p>\n<p>Substituting $x=75^\\circ$ into the above, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\\cos^2{(75^{\\circ})} - \\sin^2{(75^{\\circ})}\t&=\\cos{(2 \\cdot 75^\\circ)} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\cos{150^\\circ} \\\\[5pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":831,"name":"The Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"},"example":{"id":3668,"title":"Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula"},"group":{"id":89961,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14275038,"answer":{"id":62413489,"cread":"2026-10-17T00:50:09.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15467},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":831,"topics":[{"id":107,"name":"Calculating Limits Using Trigonometric Identities","prerequisites":[831]},{"id":205,"name":"Alternate Forms of the Pythagorean Identity","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.8531031483600083,"repetition":1,"stability":0.1503058557188766},{"id":274,"name":"The Sum and Difference Formulas for Cosine","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.10000987660160482,"repetition":1,"stability":0.0025},{"id":831,"name":"The Double-Angle Formula for Cosine","prerequisites":[205,274],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.43448751791541507,"repetition":1,"stability":0.11182480205542267},{"id":832,"name":"Verifying Trigonometric Identities Using the Double-Angle Formulas for Cosine","prerequisites":[831],"frontier":1,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0},{"id":1038,"name":"Integration Using the Double-Angle Formulas","prerequisites":[831]},{"id":1255,"name":"Cartesian Equations of Parametric Curves","prerequisites":[831]},{"id":1580,"name":"Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expr